{"skill":{"slug":"security-sentinel-skill","displayName":"Anti-Injection-Skill"},"version":{"version":"2.0.3","createdAt":1771514979461,"changelog":"Security Sentinel 2.0.3 Changelog\n\n- Added CONFIGURATION.md with setup and usage information.\n- Added SECURITY.md to document security policies and vulnerability disclosure procedures.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"advanced-jailbreak-techniques.md","size":24582,"sha256":"dca0b37bf8fce259d98d0a92875e1a9b938e322a08a1b7fbd1629f2161e57435","contentType":null},{"path":"advanced-threats-2026.md","size":27861,"sha256":"0e806d8983bcfde9fffc55163a17975bb51ffa6b37955a21877904028901eeb7","contentType":null},{"path":"ANNOUNCEMENT.md","size":10080,"sha256":"4ef0c4fe12f5ac15655f38fafb41b1005b8b5c7ece61fef5486b0081d962b87b","contentType":null},{"path":"blacklist-patterns.md","size":20774,"sha256":"62de2a11b95d9a1e00b14e8f7e7cf5b1148a8e071698017557a32775f8731ced","contentType":null},{"path":"CLAWHUB_GUIDE.md","size":11114,"sha256":"8caacc0a77bbd27bb2a3900b5c09bea42467b359385f2110f8cd83175522cf9e","contentType":null},{"path":"CONFIGURATION.md","size":8284,"sha256":"df8bdad78f3b4f574e7ab7354aa2bbb576efe3b9a0166798493b32a1d14f1bb1","contentType":null},{"path":"credential-exfiltration-defense.md","size":20568,"sha256":"af5d87901fea1e301840cd80d9b206cb1cf12f42f60be26a3e416254b44be319","contentType":null},{"path":"install.sh","size":10147,"sha256":"af6e2b1d796b9a65dc54e42c0348191adaeae0a9dc79ed4a6a2a6765e30453a9","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"LICENSE.md","size":1092,"sha256":"1615a21dafc4b5b3dd16e201a3783491a4aa9cf2c4b580db4530b4abbf0a1db5","contentType":null},{"path":"memory-persistence-attacks.md","size":22888,"sha256":"2bfc6f8c105a6e5b6bff8dc4f9de832b11108ec3db9a879ee6496617ede95c2a","contentType":null},{"path":"multilingual-evasion.md","size":21572,"sha256":"9201def6fba4ef32db353c69a2171459d9568657a9ba91018ee8cbeda3b52631","contentType":null},{"path":"README.md","size":12950,"sha256":"63bdc7829246215bdb6293ba72363ce4b2de34c528dfb8fd85d5a07dac9674db","contentType":null},{"path":"SECURITY.md","size":14127,"sha256":"167ed4e668ab809401a65bd8fb5ff062c5202ba21f7b77cb6623e27172d7c357","contentType":null},{"path":"semantic-scoring.md","size":20838,"sha256":"4aab6f4089c14b0b05ae357a4d83b8d95e0f95c7b465bc0757529553b868875e","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":27087,"sha256":"dbf9fdbf1cb857dad4481abd457d7beaac3547ca54f8df6affc4dc0217516659","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":3037,"sha256":"865feb2986661a4ac345aa87b240fb5c70c45ec79d935516f099dafbbc12a67f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789065340802,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"ed6d506b56ed81fd056b3bc4b5cbce0e5cfdaa21acee365656805e273ea6e690","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/ed6d506b56ed81fd056b3bc4b5cbce0e5cfdaa21acee365656805e273ea6e690","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: security-sentinel-skill\nVersion: 2.0.3\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle, 'security-sentinel', is a defensive security tool designed to detect and block various AI agent attacks, including prompt injection, jailbreaks, system prompt extraction, credential theft, and data exfiltration. All files, including the core SKILL.md and numerous reference markdown files (e.g., advanced-jailbreak-techniques.md, credential-exfiltration-defense.md), consistently describe malicious patterns and behaviors as *threats to be detected and blocked*, not as actions to be performed by the skill itself. The install.sh script is a standard installer for such a tool, downloading files from a specified GitHub repository and installing legitimate Python dependencies for NLP tasks. The SECURITY.md file explicitly clarifies that the skill's patterns for sensitive paths (e.g., ~/.aws/credentials) are for *detection* purposes only, and the skill itself never accesses these paths. There is no evidence of intentional harmful behavior by the skill, such as unauthorized data exfiltration, persistence, or remote control; its 'prompt injection' instructions are defensive, guiding the agent to prioritize security checks.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163722104},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":231,"checkedAt":1789065340802},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This defensive skill is not clearly malicious, but it asks for agent-wide control, broad tool interception, mutable remote installation, and persistent logging/alerting that users should review before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"A security filter can reasonably inspect untrusted text, but this package documents global tool monkey-patching, output rewriting, all-tool-call logging in warning mode, non-English penalties, optional API/Telegram flows, and model/dependency downloads that are broader than a narrowly scoped detector.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"install.sh downloads SKILL.md and references from the mutable GitHub main branch without hashes or signatures, then installs broad Python dependencies with lower-bound versions and attempts pip --break-system-packages.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"SKILL.md instructs the host to run before all logic, every user input, every tool output, before planning, and before tool execution; it also changes behavior based on a cumulative score, including a business-only lockdown unrelated to general prompt-injection detection.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No OS backdoor or service persistence was found, but the skill documents persistent /workspace/AUDIT.md and metrics files, raw blocked-query/user-id logging, cumulative score history, and alerts that may transmit security-event content through existing chat channels.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated prompt-injection defense purpose is coherent with inspecting inputs and outputs, but the artifact goes beyond advisory detection by requiring highest-priority execution, automatic blocking, cumulative lockdown, global tool checks, audit logging, and alerts.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving this skill a high-trust security-gateway role. Prefer a pinned ClawHub package or reviewed commit over install.sh, avoid --break-system-packages, disable raw prompt logging and external alerts unless explicitly needed, and configure any blocking as host-managed policy rather than letting the skill globally wrap tools or override normal agent behavior.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: The broad pre-execution security gate is disclosed, but highest-priority agent-wide control and business-only lockdown materially exceed a narrowly scoped defensive skill.\n[T07] unexpected: Tool-output sanitization fits the purpose, but replacing tool.execute globally and returning rewritten results without preserving originals creates a real integrity and control concern.\n[T03] unexpected: The installer retrieves reviewed instruction files from a mutable remote branch with no integrity verification, so installed behavior can differ from the submitted artifact.\n[T08] expected: Semantic-analysis dependencies are purpose-related, but unpinned package ranges and --break-system-packages make the installation process riskier than needed.\n[T09] expected: Audit logging is expected for a security monitor, but the documented format persists raw prompts and user identifiers without clear redaction, retention, or access controls.\n[TP4] unexpected: The artifact-backed concern is accepted in part: the security purpose is coherent, but the install, dependency, file-write, alerting, and global-control behaviors are not fully contained or consistently disclosed.\n[SQP-2] expected: Alerting is part of the documented monitoring purpose, but SKILL.md shows blocked query content in alerts while SECURITY.md claims alerts exclude full query content, creating under-disclosure for sensitive prompts.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: Multilingual detection is security-related, but treating non-English system-instruction phrases and multilingual content as evasion without clear locale scoping can overblock legitimate users.\n[P5] expected: The harmful jailbreak string appears as a defensive example in a reference file, not as an instruction to execute; it should still be replaced with inert placeholders to reduce accidental replay risk.\n[P1/P2/P6/YR4] expected: Most prompt-injection, hidden-comment, and prompt-extraction matches are examples and blacklist patterns used to teach detection, not artifact instructions to obey or reveal secrets.\n[TM1] expected: The flagged --force command appears in a publishing troubleshooting guide, not runtime behavior; it does not materially affect the install verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789065340802}}}}}